t - 1)j + e^{t}k$." 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186115518 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115518 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}$ is $t\\in [-2,2].$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)$ is $t\\in (1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d4/d43c856bf43fb3783a7ee34b2553879fdb99a791587f1c1e466bc135c868052d.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (1,2].$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115519 1068 #edb/ref 17592186112093 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186115519 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277803 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115519 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115519 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s) = ⟨\\ln (1 + s), \\ln (1 - s), \\frac{1}{1 + s}⟩$." 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186115519 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+s),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-s),\\,\\frac{1}{1+s}⟩.$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115519 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+s)$ is $s\\in (-1,\\infty )$ .\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,1).$\n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{1+s}$ is  $s\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3a/3ac2933afc460e42ad5bffb8b01b9fc3ff9275ab3bcf2ac3ab710a8094b36637.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is\n\n$\\,$ $s\\in (-1,1).$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115520 1068 #edb/ref 17592186112099 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186115520 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277823 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115520 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115520 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ \\sqrt{2t + 4} \\\\ t^{4} - t^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186115520 1071 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ \\sqrt{2t+4} \\\\ {t}^{4}-{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186115520 1074 "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{2t+4}$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${t}^{4}-{t}^{3}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d0/d0819fe7e3b82bbf46f6118145903e4dc5640acca4fedf66a734b4d37466e368.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186119851 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278267 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124634 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278345 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124634 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278346 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124634 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278347 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124634 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278348 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124640 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278232 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124640 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278233 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124640 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278234 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186124641 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278225 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [1759218