86129281 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278377 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278504 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278505 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278506 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278507 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278508 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278509 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278510 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129509 1068 #edb/ref 17592186126524 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129509 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278091 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129509 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129509 1071 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T$, given by\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u^{2} - 2v^{2} \\\\ u - v\\end{bmatrix}$,\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129509 1071 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129509 1074 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & -4v \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-1)-(-4v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2u+4v & <0 \\\\ 4v & <2u \\\\ v & <\\frac{1}{2}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{2}u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/09/09f7f36ecc2197cc95e1878fa22ac22367978809a5241f09886a7eb2fab071f3.png)" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129513 1068 #edb/ref 17592186126548 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129513 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277880 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129513 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129513 1071 "For the transformation $T$, defined as\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2u\\cos v \\\\ 3u\\sin v\\end{bmatrix}$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129513 1071 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129513 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$ and $y(u,v)=3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot 3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-(-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =6u({cos}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v) \\\\  & =6u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,2)}=6(1)=6.\n$$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129514 1068 #edb/ref 17592186126554 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129514 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277845 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129514 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129514 1071 "For the transformation $T$, defined as\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}e^{u + v} \\\\ e^{u - v}\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129514 1071 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ {e}^{u-v}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129514 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={e}^{u+v}$ and $y(u,v)={e}^{u-v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={e}^{u+v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & ={e}^{u-v} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-{e}^{u-v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ {e}^{u-v} & -{e}^{u-v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot (-{e}^{u-v})-{e}^{u+v}\\cdot {e}^{u-v} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2u}-{e}^{2u} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(0,-5)}=-2{e}^{2(0)}=-2.\n$$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129521 1068 #edb/ref 17592186126596 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129521 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277922 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129521 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129521 1071 "By integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, evaluate the triple integral\n$∭_(R)(x - y)e^{z}dV$\nover the rectangular box $R = {(x, y, z): 0 \\le x \\le 1,-1 \\le y \\le 0, \\ln 2 \\le z \\le 2}$." 13194139533404 17592186045585 false] [17592186129521 1071 "By integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\le z\\le 2}.$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186129521 1074 "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x-y){e}^{z}]_{z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{z=2}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)[\\frac{1}{2}(1-0)-(1-0)y]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy & =({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}-y\\,dy \\\\  & =({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-2}{2}(0-(-1)+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133814 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278258 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133814 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278259 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133815 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278269 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133824 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278392 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133824 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278395 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133824 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278402 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133824 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278405 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133824 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278409 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278450 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278502 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278511 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278514 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278355 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278421 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278439 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278440 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278451 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278453 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133920 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278568 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133920 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278569 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133920 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278570 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133920 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278571 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133920 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278572 13194139533404 17592186045585 true] [17592186133921 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278559 13194139